course: dictionary
lesson: 6246
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and «moderate» is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. These are its context, and they leave clues.
explain: «Ratings come with short words of advice, like "contains moderate violence" or "strong language", so families know why the film got its rating.» Here moderate means some, but not extreme. The film has some violence, but not a huge amount. Try swapping in medium and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The clues change the meaning. In «moderate exercise», you get warm and a bit out of breath. In «in moderation», you do not have too much. In a weather report, «moderate rain» is in the middle, not heavy and not light. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
fact: Moderate most often means not too much and not too little, somewhere in the middle.
fact: «Moderate exercise» makes you warm and a bit out of breath.
fact: «In moderation» means not too much, as with sweets or screen time.
fact: As a verb, moderate can mean to make something less strong, or to keep a debate fair and safe.
fact: Online, moderators remove unkind or unsafe posts.
exercise: «Ratings come with short words of advice, like "contains moderate violence".» What does moderate mean here? | Not allowed at all | *Some, but not extreme | Very frightening and gory | Hidden from view
exercise: Mum says, «Do some moderate exercise today.» What does she mean? | Exercise so hard you cannot move | Exercise only on Sundays | *Exercise that makes you warm and a bit out of breath | No exercise at all
exercise: In a weather report, what do «moderate winds» mean? | Warm, sunny breezes | *Winds in the middle, not too strong and not too weak | Completely still air | Very strong gusts that blow things over
test: «Eat sweets in moderation.» What does in moderation mean? | Eat as many as you want | Eat them in the dark | *Not too many | Only on birthdays, and never anything else
test: A moderator keeps a debate going. What does moderate mean in «moderate a debate»? | Write a loud speech for the class | *Keep the discussion fair and safe | Cancel the debate forever | Shout over everyone until they stop
exam: What does moderate mean in «moderate heat»? | Hot one moment and cold the next | Burning hot, like a bonfire | Freezing cold, like ice | *Not too hot and not too cold
